  "_about": "Grazing is ox stamina gained per day, Jan..Dec. Weather weights per season: clear, hot, windy, cold, frost, rain, storm. General climate pattern [recall, verify]; numbers invented. fever = chance a day, Jan..Dec, that each person catches malaria in this country; fly = share of the oxen, cattle and horses that die of the tsetse fly (nagana) a day. Both are estimates [estimate] anchored on Tregardt's party (research.md sections 16 and 19): crossing the lowveld in Feb-Mar 1838 most of them caught the fever and about half died within the year, and nearly all their cattle died within weeks. The dry winter was the safe season (the Tsonga traders crossed then).",
